{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-b14c224cd3c8c34d", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# SpotSound: Enhancing Large Audio-Language Models with Fine-Grained Temporal Grounding\narXiv: 2604.13023\nAuthors: Luoyi Sun, Xiao Zhou, Zeqian Li, Ya Zhang, Yanfeng Wang, Weidi Xie\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: audio_understanding\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We endow large audio-language models with robust temporal grounding via a training objective that directly suppresses hallucinations on non-existent events.\n  2. We incorporate temporal information by interleaving timestamp tokens with audio tokens to provide the fine-grained resolution needed to capture precise timing and duration.\n  3. We construct a challenging temporal audio grounding benchmark, SpotSound-Bench, filling a gap in evaluation resources for long-duration, realistic temporal reasoning.\n  4. We demonstrate state-of-the-art performance across multiple temporal grounding benchmarks while maintaining strong accuracy on standard sound event detection tasks.\n\nTags: LALM, LALM/理解型, Eval, Eval/基准\n=====\n# LAT-Audio: Precise Temporal Awareness for Long-Form Audio in Large Audio Language Models\narXiv: 2604.22245\nAuthors: \nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: audio_understanding\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Construction of LAT-Chronicle, a 1.2k hour long-form audio dataset with multi-dimensional temporal annotations across diverse real-world scenarios in Chinese and English.\n  2. Development of LAT-Bench, the first human-verified benchmark supporting audio up to 30 minutes while covering three core tasks: Dense Audio Caption, Temporal Audio Grounding, and Targeted Audio Caption.\n  3. Proposal of LAT-Audio, a framework that formulates long-form audio temporal awareness as a progressive global-to-local reasoning paradigm with Think-With-Audio Chain-of-Thought.\n  4. Open-sourcing of the dataset, benchmark, and model to facilitate future research on long-form audio temporal awareness.\n\nTags: LALM, LALM/理解型, Agent, Agent/Action", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "fd960e0c-7cf9-489d-8366-7a1f9f501bb2", "uuid": "3891d22a-4a7c-414c-9f56-7a28e763ee07", "timestamp": "2026-07-29T06:04:50.176Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# SpotSound: Enhancing Large Audio-Language Models with Fine-Grained Temporal Grounding\narXiv: 2604.13023\nAuthors: Luoyi Sun, Xiao Zhou, Zeqian Li, Ya Zhang, Yanfeng Wang, Weidi Xie\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: audio_understanding\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We endow large audio-language models with robust temporal grounding via a training objective that directly suppresses hallucinations on non-existent events.\n  2. We incorporate temporal information by interleaving timestamp tokens with audio tokens to provide the fine-grained resolution needed to capture precise timing and duration.\n  3. We construct a challenging temporal audio grounding benchmark, SpotSound-Bench, filling a gap in evaluation resources for long-duration, realistic temporal reasoning.\n  4. We demonstrate state-of-the-art performance across multiple temporal grounding benchmarks while maintaining strong accuracy on standard sound event detection tasks.\n\nTags: LALM, LALM/理解型, Eval, Eval/基准\n=====\n# LAT-Audio: Precise Temporal Awareness for Long-Form Audio in Large Audio Language Models\narXiv: 2604.22245\nAuthors: \nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: audio_understanding\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Construction of LAT-Chronicle, a 1.2k hour long-form audio dataset with multi-dimensional temporal annotations across diverse real-world scenarios in Chinese and English.\n  2. Development of LAT-Bench, the first human-verified benchmark supporting audio up to 30 minutes while covering three core tasks: Dense Audio Caption, Temporal Audio Grounding, and Targeted Audio Caption.\n  3. Proposal of LAT-Audio, a framework that formulates long-form audio temporal awareness as a progressive global-to-local reasoning paradigm with Think-With-Audio Chain-of-Thought.\n  4. Open-sourcing of the dataset, benchmark, and model to facilitate future research on long-form audio temporal awareness.\n\nTags: LALM, LALM/理解型, Agent, Agent/Action", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
